{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773266373,"nonce":"R/CbGkqctfg6avXtikS+3uPuXF8=","title":"Extract business requirements into docs/requirements.md with test traceability","message":"## Goal\n\nCreate `docs/requirements.md` — a concise list of business-level requirements for nightshift. Each requirement describes **what** the system must do from a user/stakeholder perspective, not how it's implemented. Map every test to a requirement and flag gaps.\n\n## Sources\n\n- `SPEC.md` — distill observable behaviors from implementation details\n- git-bug issues (closed and open) — feature motivations\n- Existing test files — some encode implicit requirements\n\n## Format\n\nKeep it short. Each requirement gets:\n- **ID**: `REQ-xxx`\n- **One-line description**\n- **Tests**: test files that verify it\n- **Status**: `covered` | `partial` | `untested`\n\nExample:\n```\n### REQ-005: Human Q\u0026A\nThe agent can ask blocking questions to a human and resume work when answered.\n\n- **Tests:** test_marker_reliability.py, test_post_container.py\n- **Status:** covered\n```\n\n## Granularity\n\nRequirements describe user-visible behaviors, not implementation mechanisms. The right level:\n\n- \"The system auto-resumes when the agent hits context limits\" — yes\n- \"SessionRunner builds resume prompt with checkpoint history\" — no (implementation)\n- \"Agent work is reviewed before merging\" — yes\n- \"@@DONE@@ sets status to waiting:review\" — no (implementation)\n\nExpect ~15-25 requirements total.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n1. `docs/requirements.md` with all requirements numbered\n2. Traceability summary: which test files cover which requirements\n3. **Orphan tests** section — tests that don't map to any requirement, with notes on whether they need a requirement added or should be removed\n4. **Untested requirements** section — requirements with no test coverage\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Don't rewrite SPEC.md\n- Don't write missing tests — just identify gaps\n- Don't restructure test files\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Every user-facing capability of nightshift has a REQ-xxx\n- [ ] Every test file maps to at least one REQ-xxx (or is flagged as orphan with rationale)\n- [ ] Every REQ-xxx lists its tests (or is flagged as untested)\n- [ ] Document reads as an executive summary, not a spec","files":null}]}